      <Desc>The Oligonucleotide Therapeutics Society program is delivered through a four-day professional meeting featuring scientific presentations by speakers from industry, academia, and students in the field of oligonucleotide therapeutics. An organizing committee develops the program content and agenda and decides which speakers will present their research. Some speakers are invited directly while others are invited based on submitted abstracts that summarize their research. The organizing committee ensures that the information being presented is current, relevant, and of interest to all constituent groups represented by the society's membership. The program also includes between 250-300 posters which are presented on current research in the industry. Up to forty Poster Awards are given to the best posters chosen by a selection committee of reviewers made up of members of the Board of Directors and Scientific Advisory Committee. Between 35-50 travel grants are awarded annually to students and postdocs to assist with their travel expenses to the meeting. Additional annual awards include two scholarships named for one of the society's founding members, a young investigator award from the publisher of the society's official journal, and a lifetime achievement award.</Desc>
